\section{Most of these models do not return minutes}{


They return \strong{iRT} - indexed retention time, a dimensionless scale anchored to standard
peptides. Only \code{Chronologer_RT} returns absolute minutes. An iRT of 130 looks exactly like a
plausible 130-minute gradient, so check \code{retention_time_unit} before plotting anything against
a real gradient, and fit the iRT-to-minutes line on shared peptides first.

}
